  "articleBody": "Thinking about tackling that door frame installation yourself to save a few bucks? It's tempting, but there are some hidden dangers that can pop up if you're not super experienced. One of the most common mistakes we see is incorrect rough-opening measurements. If that opening isn't just right, your door won't fit properly, leading to gaps, sticking, or just a wonky look. Another big issue is getting the frame out of square. An out-of-square frame means your door will never hang correctly, no matter how much you adjust it. Then there's the header support; if it's inadequate, especially in a load-bearing wall, you could be compromising the structural integrity of your home. Yikes! People also often forget to account for the specific type of door they're installing, which can lead to problems with hardware fitting or the door operating smoothly. These aren't just cosmetic issues; they can affect insulation, security, and the overall longevity of your door. For peace of mind and a perfectly functioning door, it's often worth calling in professionals like HH Remodeling LLC, who have the experience to get it right the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}